---
title: Chicken parmesan
servings: 6
tags: [italian, chicken]
cuisine: italian
time: 1 hour 30 minutes
source: Chicken Parmigiana by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/chicken-parmigiana/
---

Halve the @chicken breasts{3}(300 g each) horizontally into 6 thin pieces.
Season both sides with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and
@Italian seasoning{1/2%tsp}, and refrigerate ~{30%minutes}.

== Sauce ==

Heat the @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #saucepan{} over medium heat. Cook the
@garlic{2%cloves}(finely minced) and
@yellow onion{1/4%cup}(very finely chopped, or shallot) ~{3%minutes}, until the
onion is translucent. Stir in the @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}(optional) and
@Italian seasoning{1/4%tsp} for ~{15%seconds}.

Add the @dry white wine{1/4%cup}(optional), turn up the heat and bubble until
mostly gone. Add the @tomato puree{400%g}(passata),
@chicken broth{1/2%cup}(or water), @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and
@black pepper{1/4%tsp}. Cover and simmer on low ~{10%minutes}, until thickened.
Keep warm.

== Crumbing and frying ==

Heat the oven to 180°C (350°F). Set out three #shallow bowls{}: one with the
@all-purpose flour{1/3%cup}; one with the @eggs{2} beaten with
@garlic{1%clove}(minced), @kosher salt{1/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and
@Italian seasoning{1/4%tsp}; and one with the @panko{1.5%cups} mixed with
@parmesan{1/2%cup}(finely grated), @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and
@black pepper{1/4%tsp}.

Flour each piece of chicken and shake off the excess, coat it in egg, then press
it into the crumbs.

Set a #wire rack{} over a paper-towel-lined tray. Heat 1.5 to 2 cm of the
@olive oil{2%cups}(for frying, or vegetable oil) in a #skillet{} over
medium-high heat to 180°C (350°F). Fry two or three pieces at a time,
~{2%minutes} on the first side and ~{1.5%minutes} on the second. Drain on the
rack.

== Assembly ==

Lay the chicken on a #baking tray{}. Spoon 1/3 cup of sauce over each piece,
leaving the edges uncovered so they stay crisp. Scatter with
@basil{10%leaves}(roughly chopped), then the @mozzarella{2%cups}(shredded), then
@parmesan{3/4%cup}(finely grated), and drizzle with
@olive oil{1%tbsp}(extra virgin).

Bake ~{15%minutes}, until the cheese melts and browns in spots. Scatter with
more @basil{5%leaves}(chopped, optional) and serve at once.

> To skip frying, bake the crumbed chicken at 200°C (390°F) ~{15%minutes}
> before saucing.
